# QuadRover SITL for the L2 closed loop: loaded after rover.parm, quadrover.parm and the robot's
# hardware params (quadrover_from_pixracer.param). Only what SITL needs differently from the robot.
#
# MAVLink ports (SITL TCP 5760 + 2n for SERIALn): SERIAL0 5760 MAVROS, SERIAL1 5762 render node
# (SIM_STATE), SERIAL2 5763 checks. The hardware file has SERIAL2 off.
SERIAL0_PROTOCOL 2
SERIAL1_PROTOCOL 2
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 2
# No transmitter or ground station in SITL: their failsafes would fire at once.
FS_THR_ENABLE 0
FS_GCS_ENABLE 0
# SITL's own analog downward rangefinder and flow sensor in place of the MAVLink ones (ToF ring, flow board).
RNGFND1_TYPE 1
RNGFND1_MIN 0
RNGFND1_MAX 40
RNGFND1_SCALING 12.12
RNGFND1_PIN 0
FLOW_TYPE 10
SIM_FLOW_ENABLE 1
# No GPS on the robot.
GPS1_TYPE 0
SIM_GPS1_ENABLE 0
# Planner flights (D4): a stale Guided target stops the vehicle after 0.5 s.
Q_GUID_TIMEOUT 0.5
# The render node puts the lidar 0.178 m (7 in, measured) ahead of the FC; the robot's file says 0.22.
VISO_POS_X 0.178
# The robot's CAN ports: SITL simulates CAN over UDP multicast, which a loopback-only namespace
# cannot route (SITL exits "udp connect failed on port 20721"); no CAN devices are simulated anyway.
CAN_P1_DRIVER 0
CAN_P2_DRIVER 0
# The robot's ToF ring is a proximity sensor (PRX1_TYPE 2); SITL has none ("PRX1: No Data" blocks arming).
PRX1_TYPE 0
# The robot's 6S pack (arm 22.1 V, low 21.6 V, critical 21 V, failsafe actions kept) on SITL's simulated
# analog monitor (the robot's monitor type 9 is not simulated). SITL's motors give thrust in proportion
# to SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE: the model is sized for its default 12.6 V, and 25.2 V doubles its thrust (it shot
# to 20-30 m on a 1.5 m takeoff, motors on the floor). So the thresholds are halved instead.
BATT_MONITOR 4
BATT_ARM_VOLT 11.05
BATT_LOW_VOLT 10.8
BATT_CRT_VOLT 10.5
